# How to add/extend brand files

Every brand file (`vivo.json`, `oppo.json`, `moto.json`, `apple.json`, etc.) follows this order top to bottom:

**deviceType → brand → boxes[] → box → models[] → model → stock[] → place + qty**

Copy `_template.json`, rename it to the brand (e.g. `samsung.json`), and fill it in. Everything below shows how to extend each level.

---

## 1. Adding a brand (new file)

Just duplicate the template. One file = one brand.

```json
{
  "deviceType": "Android",
  "brand": "Samsung",
  "boxes": [ ... ]
}
```

`deviceType` is usually `"Android"` or `"iOS"` — keep it consistent across brands of the same OS, since the app filters by this field.

---

## 2. Adding more boxes to a brand

Add another object inside the `"boxes"` array. A brand can have as many boxes as you actually have physical boxes for it.

```json
"boxes": [
  { "box": "Vivo 1", "models": [ ... ] },
  { "box": "Vivo V Box", "models": [ ... ] },
  { "box": "Vivo T Box", "models": [ ... ] }
]
```

---

## 3. Adding more models inside ONE box (the mixed-box case)

This is the case you mentioned — when a box doesn't have enough of one model alone, so a few different models sit together in it. Just add more objects to that box's `"models"` array:

```json
{
  "box": "Oppo A-series Box",
  "models": [
    { "series": "A-series", "model": "A5", "displayCode": "2201", "stock": [ ... ] },
    { "series": "A-series", "model": "A9", "displayCode": "2005", "stock": [ ... ] }
  ]
}
```

Each model inside a shared box still tracks its own stock separately — the box is just where they physically sit.

---

## 4. Adding/removing places (Home, Shop A, Shop B, ...)

Every model's `"stock"` array should list the same set of places for consistency, even if qty is `0` there:

```json
"stock": [
  { "place": "Home", "qty": 3 },
  { "place": "Shop A", "qty": 5 },
  { "place": "Shop B", "qty": 0 },
  { "place": "Shop C", "qty": 2 }
]
```

If you add a brand-new place (like `"Shop C"`), add it to every model's stock array across all brand files so the app's place filter/list stays complete.

---

## 5. Quick checklist when adding a new model

- [ ] Is it going into an existing box, or does it need a new box?
- [ ] `series`, `model`, `displayCode` filled in (displayCode = the model number, e.g. `1802`)
- [ ] `stock` array covers every place you track, with correct `qty`

---

Once you've practiced with a few brands using this template, send them over and I'll fold them into the real data set — and then we can update `app.js`/`admin.js` to actually read this box-first structure.*/
